This product depends on @misofm/engine@0.2.5. The reviewed integration archive
was packed from misofm/engine commit
1646a6a1bd0011cc2b5480283bf498b27be460e5 with SHA256
c26208470b5409ad789085d251d94bdf1117b32dcd3b5e544f8696dffffe3d4d.
This records reviewed source/archive identity, not registry publication.

The transport SHA-256 implementation and verified-store/session-gate invariants
were adapted from the issue-authorized misofm/engine stem-store baseline at
commit bd7f330a9773ce43bb077f0e6d5c8fc30fe9e27c.

Canonical PCM identity verification uses hash-wasm 4.12.0 under the MIT
License. Its complete license text is included in
`dist/codec-licenses/hash-wasm-LICENSE`.

Canonical PCM identity verification also embeds the official Rust BLAKE3 1.8.7
implementation with the wasm32_simd feature. Its CC0 and Apache 2.0 license
texts, including the Apache LLVM exception, are included verbatim in
`dist/codec-licenses/blake3-LICENSE_CC0`,
`dist/codec-licenses/blake3-LICENSE_A2`, and
`dist/codec-licenses/blake3-LICENSE_A2LLVM`.
The runtime dependencies linked into that Wasm artifact retain their verbatim
licenses under the `blake3-arrayvec-*`, `blake3-cfg-if-*`, and
`blake3-constant_time_eq-*` files in the same directory.

The bounded PCM pump and its serialized Worker self-drive/control queue were
adapted from that same authorized Engine baseline. Ring allocation/writing,
scratch boot and the AudioWorklet feed now delegate to the Engine SDK. The
prior adapter copies of the MSB1 allocation/reader and feed mechanism came from
misofm/app commit 7485693e9bbcf2f65a91a4e5950e22d678d99062; their retained
attribution is shipped with the SDK that now owns these implementations.

This product redistributes the pinned libFLAC 1.5.0 WebAssembly decoder owned
and published by `@misofm/codec@0.1.0`. The packed adapter also bundles the
public codec's Effect-powered worker implementation. The complete codec,
Effect, and hash-wasm license texts, together with the codec's third-party notices and
licenses for the bundled Wasm asset, are included in `dist/codec-licenses/`.
